                <pb facs="0968" n="852" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg852"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.41/126.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Letcher to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Chihuahua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-02-25">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 25, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s February 21. I regret to inform you that telegraphic report of a
                    statement obtained from Villa was suppressed in telegraph office here. Substance
                    is that the Englishman addressed Villa menacingly and abusively and the latter
                    stepped behind him under the pretext of opening door, felt for and discovered
                    pistol on Benton and then sprang upon him. He declared that he himself ordered
                    execution and said nothing of a court martial. The statement was verbal but a
                    written one was promised but has not been received. Villa manifested much
                    irritation and said that he was tired of being worried <pb facs="0969" n="853"
                        xml:id="pg853"/> about such trifling matters and that he would cut the wires
                    to prevent being so troubled further. I am sure that he does not understand
                    gravity of the case and his advisers can do nothing with him.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Letcher</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
